i915/pxp: only run plane key check for protected framebuffers

check_protection() called intel_pxp_key_check() for every plane on
DISPLAY_VER >= 11, regardless of whether the framebuffer object was
protected. On Alder Lake-P this has two bad effects:

  1. When the PXP session never becomes active (consumer CSME firmware
     that doesn't provision PXP), every atomic commit logs
     "PXP key_check failed: PXP not active!" via drm_err_ratelimited.

  2. With CONFIG_DRM_I915_PXP=n, intel_pxp_init() never allocates
     i915->pxp, so i915->pxp is NULL. intel_pxp_key_check(NULL, ...)
     then dereferences pxp->ctrl_gt in the "not active" error path,
     causing a NULL-pointer kernel panic during display bring-up at boot.

Non-protected planes always resolve to decrypt=false / force_black=false,
so guard the key check with i915_gem_object_is_protected(). This removes
the log spam, keeps PXP fully functional for real protected content, and
avoids the NULL deref.
Index: v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
===================================================================
--- v6.12.orig/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
+++ v6.12/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
@@ -2124,10 +2124,22 @@ static void check_protection(struct inte
 	if (DISPLAY_VER(i915) < 11)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Only protected framebuffers need a PXP key check. Calling
+	 * intel_pxp_key_check() for every plane spams the log with
+	 * "PXP not active!" on systems where the PXP session never comes up,
+	 * and dereferences a NULL i915->pxp when CONFIG_DRM_I915_PXP is off.
+	 * Non-protected planes always resolve to decrypt=false/force_black=false.
+	 */
+	if (!i915_gem_object_is_protected(obj)) {
+		plane_state->decrypt = false;
+		plane_state->force_black = false;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	key_ret = intel_pxp_key_check(i915->pxp, obj, false);
 	plane_state->decrypt = key_ret == 0;
-	plane_state->force_black = i915_gem_object_is_protected(obj) &&
-		!plane_state->decrypt;
+	plane_state->force_black = !plane_state->decrypt;
 
 	if (plane_state->force_black)
 		drm_err_ratelimited(&i915->drm,
